0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T06:19:53-08:00","id":785357,"title":"","content":"Son shiuld I ahoor myself in private? Or in front of oeople so someone cares?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T07:39:21-08:00","id":785383,"title":"","content":"Does anyone care? Or should i just open my wrists without the announcement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T10:52:20-08:00","id":785470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/391092-the-drunk-thread?p=785383#post785383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone care? Or should i just open my wrists without the announcement?</div> </div> </div> </div>We do care that you are here, feel free to vent whatever comes up. Post on either thread or both as you prefer - i suppose answers in the Mental Health one might be more sensible or at least more coherent, though that's a guess more than anything.<br /> <br /> I just ask that you be a little patient, as people to have a little patience, some of us are also venting or spouting crap as it comes along and that can make some of us a bit slow to read and or answer.<br /> <br /> Ah, if you go for both threads, try not to answer the question of one thread with a post in the other, i confused myself with that kind of crossing the streams crap once.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/391092-the-drunk-thread?p=670614#post670614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fucking bots and spammers aren't topping this forum. Fuck them and their SkyNet.<br /> <br /> I managed to find beautifully aged, single distillery pure blue agave tequila for under 15 dollars. Sauza. These guys make Cuervo look like fucking amateurs. High quality tequila, from silver to gold to practically agave plant moonshine, they never fail to impress.<br /> <br /> I took my first sip of the Sauza Blue, and my immediate thought was &quot;this almost tastes like honey&quot; almost immediately followed by a Scion inspired image of Quetzalcoatl just bursting into the halls of the Norse Aesir and shouting &quot;GUYS!! You remember that honey-booze stuff you were going on about?? I totally just jumped the shark on that one. Best part: no bees! Seriously, come over. Huitzilopochtli has been dancing to an 80s mix CD with a lampshade on his head for 20 minutes straight. You NEED to try this shit. We should call it something...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Blue Silver or Blue Reposado? No, wait, whatever better try out both - not together, guy needs to properly savor each flavor. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-13-2015, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T19:35:30-08:00","id":785701,"title":"","content":"The blue silver is cheaper, generally, but comparable to or better than good Cuervo silver as is their blue Gold in comparison to Cuervo gold. It's definitely sharper, though. It's got an olivey, almost nutty aftertaste, but it's a SHOT tequila. Good for a mixer, too, but it's got that &quot;yowzah&quot; kinda pop when poured as a simple shot.. The Blue Reposada, sometimes labeled as Sauza Blanco (round, shorter bottle) is pure BLUE agave (the others are all pure Agave, but not all the blue breed) and smoother. Good as a tequila alternative to a &quot;sipping&quot; whiskey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T19:36:19-08:00","id":785702,"title":"","content":"I bought a bottle of each tonight, in case you're wondering. Because I'm amazing at dealing with life.<br /> <br /> The Blanco, btw, is also sub-labeled and often completely relabeled as 100 A\u00f1os, with Sauza in smaller print. The Blanco/Cien A\u00f1os has the more honeyed aftertaste. I'm guessing because of the purely blue agave sugar in its production, as opposed the nuttier/olive-reminiscent aftertaste I find in the silver and gold, which includes agave syrups from multiple breeds on a few plantations/agave kilns that work with Sauza around the Tequila area of Jalisco. Still good tequila.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 12-13-2015, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T22:08:34-08:00","id":787858,"title":"","content":"This thread has kinda just become a weird Dracula-esque journal type story of me descending into alcoholism. I think this'll be my last post here.