a slightly lower alcohol content (40.5% ABV as opposed to 50.5% ABV)<br /> <br /> I love whiskey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T22:09:44-07:00","id":1115796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/391092-the-drunk-thread?p=921345#post921345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heathen, you left Summer Shandy off the list. Good day to you sir, I say good day!</div> </div> </div> </div>By the way, I have tried it, and while I have had much better beers now, it must be pointed out this is a solid as grocery store beers go. My only regret is I don't have more spare cash for it.<br /> <br /> Of course, if I had more spare cash, I'd buy more Odell's, honestly. Much as I like Summer Shandy, Easy Street's even better, and 90 Shilling's pretty much my go to.<br /> <br /> Also, You'd think alcohol and coffee would be a writer's dream, right? Alcohol to get the words flowing, caffeine to pin it like butterflies to the corkboard.<br /> <br /> Nope. I actually don't have a lot of success with writing when drinking, actually. Not bad for the dreaming, but even casual drinking doesn't quite facilitate serious textual manifestations.<br /> <br /> Barring casual conversation, of course.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, yes, I am aware of the Oatmeal's thingy on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-14-2017, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T22:16:46-07:00","id":1115800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/391092-the-drunk-thread?p=1102264#post1102264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just bought a bottle of Wild Turkey 81 a day or two ago. So far, it's very enjoyable. I would've got a bottle of Wild Turkey 101, but my local ABC Store was sold out. However, Wild Turkey 81 is just as good and is a little more mellow due to a slightly lower alcohol content (40.5% ABV as opposed to 50.5% ABV)<br /> <br /> I love whiskey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't tried 81, but I am with you on 101.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T22:44:14-07:00","id":1115809,"title":"","content":"The mandarin flavor of Jarritos soda is probably my favorite Mexican import. I also highly recommend their strawberry and lime flavors.<br /> I could drunk the fuck outta some Jarritos.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://jarritos.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://jarritos.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Jarritos-Familia-Cooler.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://jarritos.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> Jarritos | The Official Drink of Tacos </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://jarritos.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://jarritos.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Super Good Mexican Sodas, bringing the taste, color, and spirit of Mexico to the world&mdash;one bottle at a time. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T23:06:07-07:00","id":1115817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/391092-the-drunk-thread?p=1115809#post1115809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mandarin flavor of Jarritos soda is probably my favorite Mexican import. I also highly recommend their strawberry and lime flavors.<br /> I could drunk the fuck outta some Jarritos.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://jarritos.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://jarritos.com/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>But what, dear, what would you pair it with, particularly if one was not fond of sweet?<br /> <br /> (Despite some of my posts, I am not particularly enamoured by sweet. Sour, even bitter, yes. Sweet, not so much. Read into my character as you will-I imagine you will not find much that my previous writing has not revealed.*)<br /> <br /> *Typing while drunk somewhat drunk always a somewhat balletic response in me. This is not a trait I imagine solely belongs to drunk me, upon reflection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T23:06:09-07:00","id":1115818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/391092-the-drunk-thread?p=1115796#post1115796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, You'd think alcohol and coffee would be a writer's dream, right? Alcohol to get the words flowing, caffeine to pin it like butterflies to the corkboard.<br /> <br /> Nope. I actually don't have a lot of success with writing when drinking, actually. Not bad for the dreaming, but even casual drinking doesn't quite facilitate serious textual manifestations.<br /> <br /> Barring casual conversation, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has been my experience as well. Caffeine gives me much-needed focus for writing, alcohol just leaves me even more distracted than usual.<br /> <br /> I <i>did</i> manage to write a script while drunk once, and it turned out pretty well after some revision. I'm pretty sure it only worked because it was a deeply personal story that I really wanted to tell, but wouldn't allow myself to. Everything good about the script was in spite of the booze, all it actually did was take away my ability to stop myself from writing what I wanted to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T06:17:16-07:00","id":1115912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/391092-the-drunk-thread?p=1115809#post1115809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mandarin flavor of Jarritos soda is probably my favorite Mexican import. I also highly recommend their strawberry and lime flavors.<br /> I could drunk the fuck outta some Jarritos.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://jarritos.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://jarritos.com/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer their pinneaple and mango. Delicious!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T08:19:18-07:00","id":1115950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div